| 1 | 3,5,7,11,17,19,23 | 23,21,19,15,9,7,3 | 79,131,183,287,443,495,599 | various | None integer |
| 2 | 3,5,7,11 | 20,16,12,4 | 79,131,183,287 | — | None |
| 3 | 3,5,7 | 17,11,5 | 79,131,183 | — | None |
| 4 | 3,5 | 14,6 | 79,131 | — | None |
| **5** | **5** | **1** | **131** | **131** | **Yes ✓** |
| 6,7,8 | 3 | 8,5,2 | 79 | — | None |

**Only solution: (p, q) = (5, 131).** Verify: 26·131−1 = 3405 = 5·681 ✓; 26·5+1 = 131 ✓.

## Case B: ab < 676 (so a < 26, b > 26)

Let d = 676 − ab > 0. Then p = (b−26)/d, q = (26−a)/d, so d | (b−26) and d | (26−a). Writing a = 26 − dq (with dq ≤ 25):

$$p = \frac{26q - 1}{26 - dq}$$

I enumerate all primes q ≥ 3 and d ≥ 1 with dq ≤ 25:

