| **1** | **23** | **3** | **597** | **199** | **Yes ✓** |

**Solutions: (p, q) = (7, 3), (19, 11), (199, 23).**

Verify:
- (7, 3): 26·3−1 = 77 = 7·11 ✓; 26·7+1 = 183 = 3·61 ✓
- (19, 11): 26·11−1 = 285 = 19·15 ✓; 26·19+1 = 495 = 11·45 ✓
- (199, 23): 26·23−1 = 597 = 199·3 ✓; 26·199+1 = 5175 = 23·225 ✓

## Completeness

Both cases are **fully enumerated** — the parametrization $p = (26-b)/(ab-676)$, $q = (a-26)/(ab-676)$ is exact (no approximation), and the divisibility constraints D | (26−b) ≤ 25 (Case A) and d | (26−a) ≤ 25 with dq ≤ 25 (Case B) bound all parameters to finite, exhaustively checked ranges. The case ab = 676 yields 26(q−p) = 1, impossible.

